## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + NEW SLICE benchmark/external/, benchmark/judge/, benchmark/evolve/
spine step:       workflow (run.py cell loop) + infra (native checkout and env builder, result store)
public interface: external.ExternalTask(Task).prepare(workdir) / check_correctness(result_text, repo_path) / grade_details() -> dict  (F-1)
public interface: Task.prepare(workdir) and Task.grade_details() optional hooks, called by run.py when present  (F-1)
public interface: external.featurebench.load(instance_id, data_rev) / external.swebench_ml.load(instance_id, data_rev) -> ExternalTask  (F-1)
public interface: external.preflight.admit(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict; external.contamination.scan(sidecar_path, task) -> bool  (F-1)
public interface: baselines.run_key(cell) -> str; baselines.lookup(key) -> Row | None; baselines.store(row)  (F-3)
public interface: run.py --panel PATH --max-usd FLOAT --cell-estimate-usd FLOAT --candidate-sha SHA  (F-6, F-2)
public interface: panels.load_panel(path) -> Panel(cheap, dev, test)  (F-1)
public interface: judge.applicability(task) -> Label; judge.critique(row, trajectory) -> str; judge.calibrate(labels) -> Agreement  (F-5)
public interface: evolve.main(--panel, --max-usd, --max-metric-calls, --seed-sha); evolve.propose_src_patch(worktree, records) -> diff; evolve.materialize(candidate) -> sha; evolve.cascade(sha) -> (score, side_info); evolve.finish(frontier)  (F-2, F-3, F-4)
public interface: prompts/tools/search.md and prompts/tools/write.md via include_str! in src/mcp/tools/definitions.rs  (F-2)
private:          uv venv build from repo_settings; Go/Rust test-output parsers; masked-state reconstruction; trajectory sidecar format; harness digest; judge prompts; GEPA engine config; mutation allowlist; AGENTS.md regen and byte-lock literal rewrite; quota classifier and recorded OAuth fixture
crust delta:      new run.py flags (--panel, --max-usd, --cell-estimate-usd, --candidate-sha); new row fields (run_key, harness_digest, task_digest, env_fingerprint, cli_version, timeout_s, trajectory_path, pass_rate, contaminated); new Task hooks prepare and grade_details; new packages external/judge/evolve; two new prompt files; PHASE4_PLAN.md superseded
arrows:           run.py -> external, baselines, panels; evolve -> run.py, baselines, judge, panels; judge -> baselines (row and sidecar read); no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Risks

- Masked-state reconstruction by reverse-applying the gold patch is [speculating]; AC-3's round trip is the only proof, and tasks that fail it drop out.
- About six of Pareto-12 are expected to build in a local `uv` venv (sympy, metaflow, seaborn ×2, xarray, pydantic) [speculating]; the FeatureBench share of the panel may be small.
- Native execution has no network or filesystem isolation; tilth trusts absolute paths and Bash can read anywhere, so an agent can fetch the upstream fix or read the harness data directory. The contamination scan detects those known paths, not every leak.
- Whether OAuth streams carry `total_cost_usd` and `rate_limit_event` is untested [speculating]; the recorded OAuth fixture in c1 settles it, and cost falls back to `pricing.yaml` when the field is absent.
- Host toolchain drift changes results; the env fingerprint invalidates frozen baselines rather than mixing them.
- Anthropic's Consumer Terms bar automated access except via an API key "or where we otherwise explicitly permit it", while Anthropic documents `setup-token` for scripts; the exposure falls on the maintainer's account.
- Subscription quota (5-hour and weekly windows) bounds throughput; long runs will stop and resume.
- Per-instance Pareto selection chases noise on expensive rollouts; frontier re-runs cost extra budget.
- Mutating `src/` invites overfitting to a small dev split; `just check` and the held-out test split are the guards.
- Retiring the power gate removes the statistical stop; `--max-usd` limits effort but not false-positive conclusions.

## Open questions

- [TBD] Judge agreement threshold and calibration-set size (default proposal: every panel task for applicability plus 20 trajectories, Cohen's kappa ≥ 0.6).
- [TBD] Frontier re-run count and plateau window (default proposal: 3 re-runs; stop after 5 rounds without dev improvement).

## Quality gates

- `just check`: exits 0 (fmt, clippy, cargo test, `tests/mcp_v2`, `tests/scripts`, bash-guard self-test).
- `cd benchmark && python3 -m pytest tests`: exits 0, including the new `test_external.py`, `test_panels.py`, `test_baselines.py`, `test_judge.py`, `test_evolve.py`, `test_analyze.py`.
- `python3 benchmark/external/preflight.py --panel benchmark/panels/<name>.json`: every admitted task reports gold resolved, empty and tampered unresolved.

## Curds

- **c1-result-substrate** — recorded OAuth stream fixture, run key with harness digest, task digest, env fingerprint, and candidate identity, untruncated trajectory sidecar, row fields, result store, `--max-usd`, auth guard, quota stop, serial cells, PHASE4_PLAN superseded and power readout informational. Covers G-4, G-5. ACs 5, 6, 7, 8, 9. Depends on: none. Child: `bench-result-substrate` (`/root/.local/share/cheese/paulnsorensen-tilth/specs/bench-result-substrate.md`); route: not selected. State: draft.
- **c2-external-task-adapter** — `prepare` and `grade_details` hooks, native checkout, masked-state reconstruction, `uv` and Go/Rust environments, native F2P/P2P grading, contamination flag, preflight. Covers G-1, G-3. ACs 1, 2, 3, 17. Depends on: c1. State: proposed.
- **c4-model-judge** — applicability labels and analysis slicing, per-rollout critiques, calibration gate. Covers G-6. ACs 10, 11. Depends on: c1. State: proposed.
- **c3-panel-manifest** — pre-registered panel with Gin, local cherry-picks, SWE-bench Multilingual picks, admitted FeatureBench tasks, and the split lock. Covers G-2, G-3. AC 4. Depends on: c2. State: proposed.
- **c5-evolution-loop** — tool-description move to prompt files, multi-component candidate with coding-agent `src_patch` proposer, applier with allowlist and byte-lock literal rewrite, cascade, GEPA engine, delta reports, frontier re-runs, held-out scoring, draft PR. Covers G-4, G-5. ACs 12–16, 18, 19. Depends on: c1, c3, c4. State: proposed.

